<h1>Configuration</h1>
<p class="subtitle">The settings Gate currently reads, including the gaps that are easy to miss.</p>

<h2 id="locations">Files and precedence</h2>
<p>Gate can read a user file at <code>~/.config/gate/config.yaml</code> and a project file named <code>.gaterc</code> in the directory where Gate is run. It does not search parent directories. Project values override user values; supported CLI flags override the corresponding merged value for that run.</p>

<div class="warning-box"><strong><code>gate init</code> does not create <code>.gaterc</code>.</strong> It creates <code>.gateignore</code> when absent, updates <code>.gitignore</code>, and attempts to install pre-commit and pre-push hooks. Create <code>.gaterc</code> yourself if you need non-default settings.</div>

<p>The <code>output</code> and <code>severity</code> maps are merged one level deep. Other project values, including <code>rules</code> and <code>hooks</code>, replace the user-level value. Malformed YAML is reported and Gate continues with the remaining/default configuration.</p>

<h2 id="defaults">Current defaults</h2>
<div class="code-block"><span class="kw">entropy_threshold</span>: <span class="val">4.8</span>
<span class="kw">verify</span>: <span class="val">false</span>
<span class="kw">hooks</span>:
  - <span class="val">pre-commit</span>
<span class="kw">severity</span>: {}
<span class="kw">rules</span>: []
<span class="kw">max_file_size</span>: <span class="val">2MB</span>
<span class="kw">output</span>:
  <span class="kw">format</span>: <span class="val">text</span>
  <span class="kw">color</span>: <span class="val">auto</span>
  <span class="kw">context_lines</span>: <span class="val">2</span></div>

<h2 id="fields">Fields Gate uses</h2>

<h3><code>entropy_threshold</code></h3>
<p>Fallback entropy threshold for source files. The default is <code>4.8</code>. Gate currently uses fixed per-type values of <code>4.5</code> for configuration-like files and <code>5.0</code> for recognized minified files, so this setting is not a universal threshold for every file.</p>

<h3><code>verify</code></h3>
<p>Defaults to <code>false</code>. When true, scans with findings can send matched credential values to provider endpoints. The CLI tries to suppress config-driven verification when <code>GATE_PRE_COMMIT</code> is set, but generated hooks currently export a different variable (<code>GATE_HOOK_TYPE</code>). Keep verification false in hook-driven configurations until that mismatch is fixed. <code>--verify</code> opts in for a run; <code>--no-verify</code> opts out. See <a href="/gate/wiki/verification/">Credential Verification</a>.</p>

<h3><code>max_file_size</code></h3>
<p>Files above this size are recorded as skipped. Numbers are bytes; strings may use <code>B</code>, <code>KB</code>, <code>MB</code>, or <code>GB</code>. Invalid or non-positive values fall back to 2 MB. Although the CLI help currently advertises <code>--max-file-size</code>, that flag is not wired into the scan handler; use <code>.gaterc</code> for now.</p>

<h3><code>severity</code></h3>
<p>Maps a rule ID to <code>critical</code>, <code>high</code>, <code>medium</code>, <code>low</code>, or <code>ignore</code>. <code>ignore</code> removes that rule's findings. Values are not strongly schema-validated, so use only the documented strings.</p>
<div class="code-block"><span class="kw">severity</span>:
  <span class="str">high-entropy-string</span>: <span class="val">low</span>
  <span class="str">stripe-test-secret</span>: <span class="val">ignore</span></div>

<h3><code>rules</code></h3>
<p>Adds JavaScript regular-expression patterns to the built-in catalog. Each entry needs <code>id</code> and <code>pattern</code>; <code>name</code>, <code>severity</code>, and <code>remediation</code> are optional. Invalid entries are skipped with an error. Custom regexes can be slow or overbroad, so test them on representative files.</p>
<div class="code-block"><span class="kw">rules</span>:
  - <span class="kw">id</span>: <span class="str">internal-service-token</span>
    <span class="kw">name</span>: <span class="str">Internal service token</span>
    <span class="kw">pattern</span>: <span class="str">'svc_[A-Za-z0-9_-]{32,}'</span>
    <span class="kw">severity</span>: <span class="val">high</span>
    <span class="kw">remediation</span>: <span class="str">Move the token to the approved secret store</span></div>

<h3><code>output</code></h3>
<ul>
  <li><code>format</code>: <code>text</code>, <code>json</code>, or <code>sarif</code>.</li>
  <li><code>color</code>: <code>auto</code>, <code>true</code>, or <code>false</code>.</li>
  <li><code>context_lines</code>: surrounding lines in text output.</li>
</ul>
<p>JSON and SARIF scans return before Gate writes its local audit entry. Text scans are the path that currently records scan history.</p>

<h2 id="hooks">The <code>hooks</code> caveat</h2>
<p>The config loader parses a <code>hooks</code> array, but the current <code>gate init</code> and <code>gate install</code> implementations do not consult it. <code>gate init</code> attempts both pre-commit and pre-push; <code>gate install</code> installs pre-commit only. Treat <code>hooks</code> as reserved until the installer is wired to it.</p>
<div class="warning-box"><strong>Current generated-hook mismatch:</strong> generated hooks set <code>GATE_HOOK_TYPE</code>, while the CLI checks <code>GATE_PRE_COMMIT</code> for verification suppression and re-staging behavior. A project with <code>verify: true</code> can therefore make network requests from the hook, and fixer changes may not be automatically re-staged as intended.</div>

<h2 id="example">Conservative example</h2>
<div class="code-block"><span class="cmt"># .gaterc</span>
<span class="kw">verify</span>: <span class="val">false</span>
<span class="kw">entropy_threshold</span>: <span class="val">5.0</span>
<span class="kw">max_file_size</span>: <span class="val">2MB</span>

<span class="kw">severity</span>:
  <span class="str">high-entropy-string</span>: <span class="val">low</span>

<span class="kw">output</span>:
  <span class="kw">format</span>: <span class="val">text</span>
  <span class="kw">color</span>: <span class="val">auto</span>
  <span class="kw">context_lines</span>: <span class="val">2</span></div>

<div class="info-box"><strong>Check the effective behavior.</strong> Gate has no command that prints the fully merged configuration today. Keep the file small, run a fixture scan after changes, and do not assume an accepted field is used by every command.</div>

